          ]
        },
        "theorySolution": "$$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}\\color{#24282d}\\frac{1+\\frac{1}{3x}}{1-\\frac{1}{x^2}}\\\\&\\color{#268cff}=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{3x+1}{3x}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{x^2-1}{x^2}\\right)}=\\frac{3x+1}{3x}\\div\\frac{x^2-1}{x^2}\\\\&\\color{#268cff}=\\frac{3x+1}{3x}\\times\\frac{x^2}{x^2-1}\\\\&\\color{#268cff}=\\frac{x(3x+1)}{3(x-1)(x+1)}\\end{aligned}$$"
